+    # Fast-tokenizer offsets correctly retain every byte-fallback token.  The
+    # prefix-decode fallback below can assign a zero-width interval to a byte
+    # continuation (for example, an uncommon Unicode character), which would
+    # otherwise leave a hole inside one sampled action target.  Only trust the
+    # fast path when re-tokenization reproduces the sampled IDs exactly.
+    try:
